External dependencies and services
==================================

Command-line tools (all ship with a stock Omarchy install): curl, jq, iconv,
head (coreutils), sh.

Network services contacted over HTTPS (read-only GET of public status data;
no credentials required):
  - Atlassian Statuspage sites for the enabled services, e.g.
    githubstatus.com, cloudflarestatus.com, status.npmjs.org, and any
    user-configured custom service endpoint
  - AWS Health public feed   https://health.aws.amazon.com
  - AWS IP ranges            https://ip-ranges.amazonaws.com  (region discovery)

User-configured "custom services" cause the plugin to contact whatever
endpoint the user supplies; no other hosts are contacted.

Privilege boundary: the plugin makes outbound HTTPS requests, opens status-page
URLs in the user's browser via xdg-open, and persists settings only to its own
entry in ~/.config/omarchy/shell.json. It does not modify any other user
configuration.
